From: logic+security (finding logic+security-10.1) — verified HIGH by independent verifier
Subject: [PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED, NOT TESTED] Wizard step machine is decoupled from the real download: progress screen (step 2) is dead code, user gets 'starting' UI for the whole download
File: src/ui/components/SetupWizard.tsx:40

Verifier note: Verificato end-to-end: il bottone Download (SetupWizard.tsx:123) chiama finish({model}) -> POST /finish (setup.ts:374-382) che setta setupDone:true e lancia ensureLlmServer() in background FUORI dal job singleton (job resta idle, logTail vuoto). postSetup("download") non ha call site in src/ui (grep: solo dichiarazione api.ts:37). Quindi step salta 1->3 subito e la schermata 3 mostra solo testo italic senza progress/log per l'intero download (lms get, timeout 60 min). Step 2 e' irraggiungibile durante un download reale: /status ritorna downloadedModels [] quando job.state==='downloading' (setup.ts:317) -> downloaded=false -> step 1; si raggiunge solo con modello gia' presente, dove "Downloading model…" + progress bar sono falsi. jobBusy/job.logTail non possono riflettere mai un download di modello. Aggravante: un fallimento del download dentro run() tocca solo backendState, quindi il blocco downloadFailed (righe 192-196) non puo' mai attivarsi su questo path. Impatto medio-alto (onboarding primario senza progressi ne' errori) + scatta sempre su fresh install (caso standard) -> HIGH.

Proposed fix (from attacker, unapplied):
Derive the step from server truth instead of `downloaded`: `const step = status.setupDone ? 3 : status.job.state === "downloading" || status.job.state === "installing-cli" ? 2 : downloaded ? 3 : 1;` and make the Download button actually start the job: `await postSetup("download", { model }); await finish({ model });` (or have finish return before the background ensure). Server-side, keep returning the in-flight model (e.g. `downloadedModels: [...models, job.model ?? []]`) so the heuristic cannot regress to step 1 during a job.
